From dd01d28301e3632d00f9ab3362e2023b8dff3141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:26:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 123/160] common/domainset: build the domain matcher of sing
 with a fraction of its memory

domain.NewMatcher keeps the whole queue of its breadth-first walk while it
builds the trie, 24 bytes a node: a list of 100000 varied names takes it
past the memory of a router with 256 MB. Build walks a level at a time and
hands the trie to sing as a binary rule set carries it (domain.ReadMatcher).
The result is the same byte for byte (TestSameAsSing). Domain rules and the
rule-set compiler use it.

100000 varied names: 41 ms and 37 MB allocated a build, against 72 ms and
160 MB.
---
